{"tool_name":"tcr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"tcr","home":"http://imminfo.github.io/tcr/","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"TCR repertoire data analysis after preprocessing data with CDR3 extraction and gene alignment software tools such as MiTCR, ImmunoSEQ and MiGEC.","addition_date":"2018-05-24T14:52:51Z","last_update_date":"2019-02-06T14:00:44Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["2.2.1.7"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:tcr","credit":[{"email":"vdm.nazarov@gmail.com","name":"Vadim I. Nazarov","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3659-2709","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://imminfo.github.io/tcr/tcrvignette.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Rarefaction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3797"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"tcR","owner":"aotamendi.1","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s12859-015-0613-1","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 Nazarov et al.; licensee BioMed Central.Background: The Immunoglobulins (IG) and the T cell receptors (TR) play the key role in antigen recognition during the adaptive immune response. Recent progress in next-generation sequencing technologies has provided an opportunity for the deep T cell receptor repertoire profiling. However, a specialised software is required for the rational analysis of massive data generated by next-generation sequencing. Results: Here we introduce tcR, a new R package, representing a platform for the advanced analysis of T cell receptor repertoires, which includes diversity measures, shared T cell receptor sequences identification, gene usage statistics computation and other widely used methods. The tool has proven its utility in recent research studies. Conclusions: tcR is an R package for the advanced analysis of T cell receptor repertoires after primary TR sequences extraction from raw sequencing reads. The stable version can be directly installed from The Comprehensive R Archive Network (http://cran.r-project.org/mirrors.html). The source code and development version are available at tcR GitHub (http://imminfo.github.io/tcr/) along with the full documentation and typical usage examples.","authors":[{"name":"Bolotin D.A."},{"name":"Chudakov D.M."},{"name":"Komech E.A."},{"name":"Lebedev Y.B."},{"name":"Mamedov I.Z."},{"name":"Nazarov V.I."},{"name":"Pogorelyy M.V."},{"name":"Shugay M."},{"name":"Zvyagin I.V."}],"citationCount":131,"date":"2015-12-12T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"tcR: An R package for T cell receptor repertoire advanced data analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC4445501","pmid":"26017500"}],"topic":[{"term":"Immunoproteins, genes and antigens","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2830"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"tcR","home":"https://bio.tools/tcr","license":"Apache-2.0","version":"2.2.1.7","summary":"TCR repertoire data analysis after preprocessing data with CDR3 extraction and gene alignment software tools such as MiTCR, ImmunoSEQ and MiGEC.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tcr:2.2.1.7/cmd/imminfo.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":false,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":147,"citat